\title{Running sum with \code{\verb~|scan~}, and a matrix product in two dimensions}
\taxon{Example}
\date{2026-11-13}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{simd}
\tag{example}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Two uses of the less common operations. The first carries the last value of each chunk into the next. The second treats a 4 by 4 matrix as a two-dimensional vector.}
\pre{\verb~|
import core::ptr;
import core::simd;
import core::ptr::PtrArithFlag;
import std::collections::cow::vec::Vec;

// Write the running sums of `src` to `dst`, which has room for as many.
pub fn prefix_sums(src: Vec<i32>, dst: Ptr<core::ptr::Generic>) -> i32 {
    let len = src.len();
    core::object::unsafe_inc(src);
    let base = src.unsafe_data_ptr();
    let zero = simd::splat<Simd<[i32; 8]>>(0);
    let (end, carry) = while [i = 0, carry = 0] (i < len) {
        let live = simd::mask_first<Simd<[bool; 8]>>(len - i);
        let x = simd::load<Simd<[i32; 8]>>(ptr::advance<i32>(base, i as i64, PtrArithFlag::Inbounds), live, zero);
        let (sums, last) = simd::scan_add(x, carry, 0, true);
        simd::store(ptr::advance<i32>(dst, i as i64, PtrArithFlag::Inbounds), sums, live);
        (i + 8, last)
    };
    core::object::unsafe_dec(src);
    carry
}

// Row i of the result is the sum over k of a[i][k] * b[k].
pub fn matmul(a: Simd<[f32; 4, 4]>, b: Simd<[f32; 4, 4]>) -> Simd<[f32; 4, 4]> {
    let (k, out) = while [k = 0, out = simd::splat<Simd<[f32; 4, 4]>>(0.0)] (k < 4) {
        let column = simd::extract(simd::transpose(a, 1, 0), k);
        let row = simd::extract(b, k);
        (k + 1, simd::add(out, simd::outer(column, row)))
    };
    out
}
~}
\ul{
\li{\code{\verb~|scan~} is not available yet, see [prob-C421](prob-C421). \code{\verb~|scan_add(x, carry, 0, true)~} starts from \code{\verb~|carry~} and includes each lane in its own sum. In the last chunk the masked lanes were loaded as zero, so \code{\verb~|last~} is still the total.}
\li{The matrix product adds four outer products. \code{\verb~|vector.contract~} would say it in one operation; it waits for affine maps in the language, see [prob-Y593](prob-Y593).}
\li{A fixed two-dimensional vector such as \code{\verb~|Simd<[f32; 4, 4]>~} can be a record field, so a transform can be stored and passed around like any value.}
}
\p{Belongs to [SIMD vectors](design-simd-vectors). Written against the draft; not compiled.}
